"translate(80.8125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(144.90625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(175.405679 138.750888) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(67.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(132.3125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_16\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(258.259354 134.254975) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(67.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(133.5 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_17\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(341.808654 143.246801) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(67.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(113.90625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"legend_1\"><g id=\"patch_13\"><path d=\"M 42.499719 18.128 L 58.499719 18.128 L 58.499719 12.528 L 42.499719 12.528 z\n\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"text_18\"><g transform=\"translate(64.899719 18.128) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-1e\" d=\"M 621 4659 Q 621 4749 698 4749 L 1158 4749 Q 1235 4749 1235 4666 L 1235 538 Q 1235 474 1299 474 L 3514 474 Q 3590 474 3590 410 L 3590 70 Q 3590 38 3571 19 Q 3552 0 3514 0 L 710 0 Q 659 0 640 22 Q 621 45 621 90 L 621 4659 L 621 4659 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-75\" d=\"M 678 -1056 Q 493 -1056 390 -1043 Q 288 -1030 288 -973 L 288 -723 Q 288 -678 323 -659 Q 358 -640 467 -640 L 870 -640 Q 1011 -640 1126 -547 Q 1242 -454 1318 -313 Q 1395 -173 1420 -29 Q 1446 115 1402 224 L 179 3283 Q 166 3328 182 3360 Q 198 3392 250 3392 L 646 3392 Q 685 3392 710 3376 Q 736 3360 749 3322 L 1702 838 Q 1728 781 1760 781 Q 1792 781 1818 858 L 2758 3322 Q 2778 3360 2797 3376 Q 2816 3392 2848 3392 L 3149 3392 Q 3194 3392 3213 3363 Q 3232 3334 3213 3296 L 1805 -301 Q 1715 -531 1606 -678 Q 1498 -826 1360 -906 Q 1222 -986 1056 -1021 Q 890 -1056 678 -1056 L 678 -1056 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-1e\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(60.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6a\" transform=\"translate(115 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6c\" transform=\"translate(164.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a5\" transform=\"translate(203.609375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-75\" transform=\"translate(225.015625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-48\" transform=\"translate(275.71875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(333.8125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-69\" transform=\"translate(388.609375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"patch_14\"><path d=\"M 115.052219 18.128 L 131.052219 18.128 L 131.052219 12.528 L 115.052219 12.528 z\n\" style=\"fill: #c2410c\"/></g><g id=\"text_19\"><g transform=\"translate(137.452219 18.128) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-2f\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-4f\" transform=\"translate(64.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-50\" transform=\"translate(122.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6a\" transform=\"translate(146.8125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a5\" transform=\"translate(198.015625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-75\" transform=\"translate(219.421875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-48\" transform=\"translate(270.125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(328.21875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-69\" transform=\"translate(383.015625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pa9a39e2639\"><rect x=\"35.299719\" y=\"27.296\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"138.6\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Cost per bag ($)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Cost per bag rose $1.54. Freight is only +$0.15 of that, worth $0.65M on 4.35M bags: <b>10% of the $6.40M gap</b>.</p> <p>Ingredients rose $1.14 a bag, worth $4.96M: <b>77% of the gap</b>.</p> <p>Full bridge: more bags +$2.80M, higher cost per bag −$6.70M, higher fixed costs −$2.50M: −$6.40M in total. Volume growth roughly offsets the fixed-cost rise, so cost per bag is the story.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> freight is real but minor. Ingredients are the story. Let's see why they rose.</p>","note":"Both years: price $18 per bag. Bags: 4.00M → 4.35M. Fixed costs: $16.0M → $18.5M."},{"q":"Here is ingredient cost by recipe and the recipe mix. Split the ingredient increase into inflation and mix.","exhibit":{"kind":"table","headers":["","Classic","Premium"],"rows":[["Ingredient cost per bag, last year ($)","5.50","9.00"],["Ingredient cost per bag, this year ($)","5.80","10.20"],["Share of bags, last year","80%","20%"],["Share of bags, this year","65%","35%"]],"title":"Exhibit 2 · Ingredients by recipe","note":null,"align":["l","r","r"],"boldLast":false},"answer":"<p><b>Mix effect</b> (more Premium at last year's costs): (35% − 20%) × ($9.00 − 5.50) = <b>$0.525</b> a bag.</p> <p><b>Inflation</b> (each recipe got dearer): 65% × $0.30 + 35% × $1.20 = <b>$0.615</b> a bag.</p> <p>Total $1.14 ✓. Mix and inflation are roughly half each.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> Premium is succeeding with shoppers, but it earns $4.40 less per bag than Classic because it's sold at the same price. Northstar is growing its least profitable product.</p>"},{"q":"If Northstar raised only the Premium price, how much more per bag would it need to recover the full gap? Is that realistic?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Premium bags: 35% × 4.35M = 1.52M. Needed: $6.40M ÷ 1.52M = <b>$4.20 a bag</b>, about 23% on $18, assuming volume holds.</p> <p>Probably too much in one go. Premium recipes usually sell at a clear premium to standard ones, so some increase is justified, but a 23% jump risks losing shelf space.</p> <p><b>Better:</b> a $2 to $3 increase on Premium (it's still a better product), plus ingredient sourcing contracts, plus cutting trade promotions that rose $0.15 a bag.</p>"},{"q":"What would you tell the CEO in her board meeting?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Answer first: freight explains only about 10% of the fall. The real issue is that Premium, now 35% of volume, is priced like Classic while costing $4.40 more in ingredients. Then: the pricing fix, sourcing, and a test of price elasticity in one region.</p>"}],"reco":"Freight is not the main problem: it explains about 10% of the $6.4M profit fall. Most of the gap comes from ingredients, split between inflation and a shift to Premium, which sells at the Classic price but costs $4.40 more a bag to make. I recommend repricing Premium by $2 to $3 a bag, locking in ingredient contracts, and trimming trade promotions. Risk: retailers resist a price rise, so lead with the stronger recipe story. Next step: test the new Premium price in one province for eight weeks.","great":["Tests the client's hypothesis with numbers instead of accepting it","Splits ingredients into mix and inflation","Spots the pricing decision behind the mix problem","Sizes the price fix and judges whether it's realistic"],"id":26,"slug":"northstar-pet-nutrition"}